# G057 — Recipe Manager

*v2. See `recipe-manager.md` for prose: scaling as pure function, pantry-gap
as shopping list, unit compatibility enforced at ingredient level.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Weekly Meal Plan

[weekly-meal-plan @planned-recipes
    IN ORDER TO
        compute the shopping list for a week's menu
        accounting for pantry and unit compatibility
        with sarah ordering groceries and korrallan checking the schedule

    @pantry          <- [recipe-book[pantry]]
    @cumulative-need <- @planned-recipes
        folded through merge-adding @recipe:lines
        starting from {}

    @shopping <- [recipe-book[gap {required: @cumulative-need,
                                     available: @pantry}]]

    concurrent [
        <- @sarah{order groceries: @shopping}
        <- @korrallan{check cooking schedule for: @planned-recipes}
    ]
    join

    where
        every recipe id is in the recipe book
        and no shopping entry has a unit-mismatch reason
        and groceries are ordered
        || -> #meal-plan-halted @resistance:reason
]

---

## Verb Surface

[recipe-book
    new
    add-ingredient   {ingredient}
    add-recipe       {recipe}
    stock            {ingredient-id, quantity, unit}
    scale            {recipe-id, factor}
    can-make         {recipe-id, servings?}       ;; (bool, [shortage])
    shopping-list    {recipe-id, servings?}
    gap              {required, available}
    make             {recipe-id, servings?}        ;; consumes pantry
    recipes-using    {ingredient-id}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: unit compatibility as resolver-enforced invariant

[recipe-book[stock {ingredient-id: @id, quantity: @q, unit: @u}
    where
        @u is compatible with the ingredient's default unit
        (e.g. kg/g/oz for mass; ml/L/cup for volume; never mixed)
        || resists with "unit-incompatible"
]

---

## Scaling as pure function

[recipe-book[scale {recipe-id: @id, factor: @n}
    where every ingredient quantity is multiplied by @n
        producing a new Recipe value, leaving the original unchanged
]

---

## Demo

[demo
    @rb <- [recipe-book[new]]
    [recipe-book[add-ingredient {ingredient: {id: "flour", default-unit: "g"}}]]
    [recipe-book[add-ingredient {ingredient: {id: "sugar", default-unit: "g"}}]]
    [recipe-book[add-recipe {recipe: {id: "pancakes", servings: 4,
                                         lines: [{ingredient: "flour", qty: 200, unit: "g"}
                                                  {ingredient: "sugar", qty: 50, unit: "g"}]}}]]

    @doubled <- [recipe-book[scale {recipe-id: "pancakes", factor: 2}]]
    -> @doubled:lines[0]:qty        ;; -> 400 (flour)

    [recipe-book[stock {ingredient-id: "flour", quantity: 300, unit: "g"}]]
    -> [recipe-book[can-make {recipe-id: "pancakes", servings: 4}]]
    ;; -> (false, [{ingredient: "sugar", short-by: 50}])
]
